# Example htpasswd for nginx basic auth in front of the DevOps Portal
# wildcard SNI router. See docs/PUBLIC_ACCESS_DEEPAKSHARMA_LIVE.md §Phase F.
#
# GENERATE A REAL FILE (DO NOT commit the result):
#   # initial user — -c CREATES the file, -B forces bcrypt (recommended).
#   htpasswd -Bc nginx-proxy/htpasswd deepak
#   # subsequent users — drop -c (preserves existing entries).
#   htpasswd -B  nginx-proxy/htpasswd teammate
#
# The real file (`nginx-proxy/htpasswd`, no `.example`) must be gitignored.
# If nginx-proxy/.gitignore does not exist, create it with exactly:
#     htpasswd
# so any accidental commit of a real credentials file is stopped at add.
#
# Format reference (https://httpd.apache.org/docs/current/programs/htpasswd.html):
#   <username>:<bcrypt-hash>
# bcrypt hashes start with $2y$ or $2b$ and are 60 chars wide. MD5 (LEGACY,
# identified by $apr1$) is also accepted by nginx but NOT recommended in
# 2026 — too fast to brute-force.
#
# Example placeholder entries (these are NOT real — the hash is gibberish):
#deepak:$2y$10$REPLACEWITHREALBCRYPTHASHGENERATEDLOCALLYDONOTCOMMITTRUE
#teammate:$2y$10$ANOTHERPLACEHOLDERHASHREPLACEBEFOREDEPLOYINGTOPRODUCTIN
